From 8511b049d2f6a5382ba4132f8d9b75dd8dc6eb9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steve Lhomme <slhomme@matroska.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:05:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] KaxBlock: throw an exception when encountering a large track
 number

This was already done in 4457e70466dcc77984202a05525428383cb74fe3 for SCOPE_ALL_DATA
but the same should be done for SCOPE_PARTIAL_DATA.
(maybe that common code should be factorized)

Discovered by Anthropic's OSS Scanner, as vulnerability ANT-2026-82J8BC58.
---
 src/KaxBlock.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/KaxBlock.cpp b/src/KaxBlock.cpp
index cf213c9..ce2ab71 100644
--- a/src/KaxBlock.cpp
+++ b/src/KaxBlock.cpp
@@ -618,7 +618,7 @@ filepos_t KaxInternalBlock::ReadData(IOCallback & input, ScopeMode ReadFully)
         // there is extra data
         if ((TrackNumber & 0x40) == 0) {
           // We don't support track numbers that large !
-          return Result;
+          throw SafeReadIOCallback::EndOfStreamX(0);
         }
         TrackNumber = (TrackNumber & 0x3F) << 8;
         TrackNumber += *cursor++;
-- 
